# Phase 0 smoke-test samples: real corpus text harvested from third-party datasets.
# Findings and code are committed; the payload is not — it is reproducible from
# artifacts/smoke/harvest_parquet.py with the recorded seed, and several sources are
# share-alike (FineWiki, StackExchange) which we keep out of a public repo.
artifacts/smoke/samples/
artifacts/smoke/judges.jsonl
artifacts/smoke/d_labels.jsonl
artifacts/smoke/spot-check-50.jsonl

# The MTLD label cache: 11.56 GB of `_labels/` objects pulled from the us-east-2 mirror
# so the curriculum ordering can be built locally. NOT committed — it is a byte-identical
# copy of s3://edullm-corpus-use2/pretrain/edu-mix-983b/79e53d1e5e131649/_labels/, which
# is the authority, and re-fetching it is one `s3 sync`. The DERIVED artifacts (the clamp
# table, the order vector's digest, the spec and stats) are committed instead.
artifacts/final-dataset/labels_raw/
# The order vector itself: 1.68 GB of uint32. Its sha256 is recorded in CURRICULUM-SPEC.json,
# which is what a reviewer checks; the bytes are reproducible from the committed generator.
artifacts/final-dataset/curriculum/*.u32le.bin
# Intermediate memmaps (per-chunk keys, ~4 GB). Pure scratch — deleting them costs a re-run.
artifacts/final-dataset/curriculum/_scratch/
__pycache__/
